  <main id="main">
  <section class="page-banner">
    <div class="page-banner-bg" aria-hidden="true"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1505664194779-8beaceb93744?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1800&q=72" alt="" /></div>
    <div class="container">
      <p class="page-eyebrow reveal"><span class="rule"></span>Insights</p>
      <h1 class="page-title reveal">Articles, reports <em>and guides.</em></h1>
      <p class="page-lede reveal">Everything the practice publishes, in one place — articles, reports and guides across every practice area. Migrated content from resource.scp-law.com will land here alongside it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section--paper">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid-cards" id="insightList">
        <article class="card filterable reveal" id="renewable-energy-framework-2026" data-topic="energy" data-type="Article" data-author="Partner, Energy">
          <div class="card-img"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1509391366360-2e959784a276?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&q=70" alt="" loading="lazy" /></div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <p class="card-cat">12 August 2026</p>
            <h3 class="card-title">Navigating the 2026 renewable energy regulatory framework</h3>
            <p class="card-desc">Analysis of the evolving legal landscape for green energy projects and the incentives now available to international investors under the climate-resilient economy guidelines.</p>
            <a class="card-more" href="#renewable-energy-framework-2026" data-track="article:open:renewable-energy-framework-2026">Read</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card filterable reveal" id="fccpc-merger-thresholds" data-topic="competition-law" data-type="Article" data-author="Partner, Competition">
          <div class="card-img"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1590650153855-d9e808231d41?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&q=70" alt="" loading="lazy" /></div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <p class="card-cat">29 July 2026</p>
            <h3 class="card-title">What the revised FCCPC merger thresholds mean for mid-market deals</h3>
            <p class="card-desc">The revised turnover thresholds pull a class of transactions into mandatory notification for the first time. We set out who is now caught and how to plan around it.</p>
            <a class="card-more" href="#fccpc-merger-thresholds" data-track="article:open:fccpc-merger-thresholds">Read</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card filterable reveal" id="ndpa-audit-filing-guide" data-topic="tech-ai" data-type="Guide" data-author="Senior Associate, Tech & AI">
          <div class="card-img"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&q=70" alt="" loading="lazy" /></div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <p class="card-cat">15 July 2026</p>
            <h3 class="card-title">The NDPA annual audit filing: a practical guide</h3>
            <p class="card-desc">A step-by-step walkthrough of what the Commission expects in an annual audit return, the common grounds for rejection, and how to prepare the evidence file.</p>
            <a class="card-more" href="#ndpa-audit-filing-guide" data-track="article:open:ndpa-audit-filing-guide">Read</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card filterable reveal" id="living-trusts-nigerian-jurisprudence" data-topic="wealth-management-smes" data-type="Article" data-author="Partner, Private Client">
          <div class="card-img"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1560518883-ce09059eeffa?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&q=70" alt="" loading="lazy" /></div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <p class="card-cat">2 July 2026</p>
            <h3 class="card-title">Asset protection: the role of living trusts in modern Nigerian jurisprudence</h3>
            <p class="card-desc">How the courts have treated inter vivos trusts over the last decade, and what that means for families structuring succession today.</p>
            <a class="card-more" href="#living-trusts-nigerian-jurisprudence" data-track="article:open:living-trusts-nigerian-jurisprudence">Read</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card filterable reveal" id="customs-amendments-logistics" data-topic="international-trade-law" data-type="Article" data-author="Senior Associate, Trade">
          <div class="card-img"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1465447142348-e9952c393450?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&q=70" alt="" loading="lazy" /></div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <p class="card-cat">18 June 2026</p>
            <h3 class="card-title">Key amendments to customs regulations for projects and transport logistics</h3>
            <p class="card-desc">The new valuation and classification rules change the landed-cost calculation for project cargo. A summary of what moved and where the exposure now sits.</p>
            <a class="card-more" href="#customs-amendments-logistics" data-track="article:open:customs-amendments-logistics">Read</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card filterable reveal" id="workplace-arbitration-trends" data-topic="labour-employment" data-type="Article" data-author="Partner, Labour">
          <div class="card-img"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1521737604893-d14cc237f11d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&q=70" alt="" loading="lazy" /></div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <p class="card-cat">4 June 2026</p>
            <h3 class="card-title">Arbitration in the workplace: recent trends in employment dispute resolution</h3>
            <p class="card-desc">The National Industrial Court's evolving posture towards arbitration clauses in employment contracts, and how to draft for enforceability.</p>
            <a class="card-more" href="#workplace-arbitration-trends" data-track="article:open:workplace-arbitration-trends">Read</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card filterable reveal" id="digital-lending-conduct-report" data-topic="consumer-credit-dml" data-type="Report" data-author="Consumer Credit team">
          <div class="card-img"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1454165804606-c3d57bc86b40?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&q=70" alt="" loading="lazy" /></div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <p class="card-cat">20 May 2026</p>
            <h3 class="card-title">Digital lending conduct standards: a market review</h3>
            <p class="card-desc">A review of enforcement across the digital lending market, the conduct failures that attract sanction, and the controls that hold up under FCCPC scrutiny.</p>
            <a class="card-more" href="#digital-lending-conduct-report" data-track="article:open:digital-lending-conduct-report">Read</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card filterable reveal" id="pia-host-community-trusts" data-topic="energy" data-type="Report" data-author="Energy team">
          <div class="card-img"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1466611653911-95081537e5b7?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&q=70" alt="" loading="lazy" /></div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <p class="card-cat">6 May 2026</p>
            <h3 class="card-title">Host community trusts under the PIA: three years in</h3>
            <p class="card-desc">What settlors have learned about constituting, funding and governing host community development trusts, and the disputes that have emerged.</p>
            <a class="card-more" href="#pia-host-community-trusts" data-track="article:open:pia-host-community-trusts">Read</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card filterable reveal" id="transfer-pricing-defence-guide" data-topic="tax-advisory" data-type="Guide" data-author="Partner, Tax">
          <div class="card-img"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1554224154-26032ffc0d07?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&q=70" alt="" loading="lazy" /></div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <p class="card-cat">21 April 2026</p>
            <h3 class="card-title">Building a transfer pricing file that survives audit</h3>
            <p class="card-desc">Documentation is only useful if it answers the questions the revenue authority actually asks. A guide to structuring the file around likely challenge.</p>
            <a class="card-more" href="#transfer-pricing-defence-guide" data-track="article:open:transfer-pricing-defence-guide">Read</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

